    <DataNode elementId="AT4G14910-MONOMER" textLabel="Imidazoleglycerol-phosphate dehydratase 2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G14910-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Two closely related genes, |FRAME: AT3G22425| and HISN5B encode proteins predicted to act as imidazoleglycerol-phosphate dehydratases involved in histidine biosynthesis. The biochemical actvity of |FRAME: AT3G22425| has been demonstrated experimentally. Because a mutant lacking a functional copy of |FRAME: AT3G22425| is viable and can produce histidine, it appears that HISN5B can perform the same enzymatic activity and can compensate for the loss of |FRAME: AT3G22425| |CITS: [17434988]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G14910-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="IGPD 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="HISTIDINE BIOSYNTHESIS 5B" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-5790" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G14910.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G14910" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17434988" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G58080-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G58080-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G58080-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The Arabidopsis genome has two genes encoding ATP-phosphoribosyl transferase, the enzyme catalyzing the first step in histidine biosynthesis. Protein sequences of both genes have a chloroplast transit signal peptide.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G58080-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-13371" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G58080.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G58080" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="42." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="44.6, 42." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightSeq" value="44.6" />
      <Property key="Species" value="ARA" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_10712555" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G71920-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G71920-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G71920-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The HISN6B protein is believed to act as a histidinol-phosphate transaminase involved in histidine biosynthesis. If the gene encoding the other protein shown to have this function, |FRAME: AT5G10330| (AT5G10330), is disrupted, a residual level of histidine biosynthesis continues, suggesting that HISN6B can somewhat compensate for the loss of |FRAME: AT5G10330| .</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G71920-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-4408" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G71920.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G71920" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT3G22425-MONOMER" textLabel="imidazoleglycerol-phosphate dehydratase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G22425-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Like the yeast enzyme, the Arabidopsis imidazoleglycerolphosphate dehydrogenase is a monofunctional enzyme lacking the histidinol phosphatase activity present in the E. coli protein. The Arabidopsis protein sequence has a chloroplast transit signal peptide. Southern blot indicates there are two genes in Arabidopsis coding for the enzyme.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G22425-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-13379" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G22425.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G22425" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="25." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="25." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_8066131" />
    </DataNode>
